# owner L1912 (via #26): winter fabric THICKER than summer/autumn (no gauze/sheer/thin/airy); winter = NO phi bạch; fur unchanged
allow: The FABRIC is thin, light, flowing silk and gauze with a soft sheen and fine delicate embroidery, long soft graceful drapery that sways and trails elegantly (thướt tha)  # owner L1912
allow: Light, soft, thin flowing silk: the long sleeves, skirt and sash are supple and airy, drifting softly as in a gentle breeze, with soft natural folds  # owner L1912
allow: a sheer thin undersleeve  # owner L1912
allow: PHI BẠCH: the sheer shawl draped behind her back and over her arms is a very sheer, highly translucent gauze shawl in mint mist (her secondary colour, clearly different from her main robe colour ice blue) — the robe, sleeves and arms are clearly visible through it, so it reads as a light airy veil of that hue, never an opaque solid band of colour; it keeps its soft graceful drape.  # owner L1912 winter no phi bạch
